cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use SimPhy-X, please cite this software and the original SimPhy paper
  (listed under "references"); SimPhy-X is a modified version of SimPhy 1.0.2.
type: software
title: "SimPhy-X: a scalable, parallel, SimPhy-compatible phylogenomic simulator"
abstract: >-
  SimPhy-X is a modified and re-engineered version of SimPhy 1.0.2 (Mallo, de
  Oliveira Martins and Posada, 2016) that simulates species trees, locus trees
  under duplication, loss, horizontal transfer and gene conversion, and gene
  trees under the multispecies and bounded multilocus coalescent. It accepts
  SimPhy's command line unchanged. Its default compat mode writes output that is
  byte-identical to SimPhy 1.0.2 for the same command and seed at any thread
  count, with linear instead of quadratic memory; its fast mode samples the same
  model with independent per-locus random streams and without arbitrary-precision
  arithmetic, and is up to about 180 times faster on duplication/loss simulations.
authors:
  - family-names: Saha
    given-names: Anik
    affiliation: Bangladesh University of Engineering and Technology
